{
    "background_story": "Frankie was a free-spirited artist who lived life on her own terms. Growing up, she was always drawn to the unconventional and the unknown. As she traveled the world, Frankie discovered her passion for photography and began capturing the beauty of the human experience. She worked accordingly to her intuition, allowing her curiosity to guide her lens. From the vibrant streets of Tokyo to the majestic landscapes of New Zealand, Frankie's camera told the story of a world full of wonder and diversity. Her artwork was met with critical acclaim, but more importantly, it inspired others to see the world through her eyes. Frankie's life was a testament to the power of following one's instincts and living accordingly to one's true nature.",
